{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega/v6.json",
  "description": "Upstream's `adjustSpatial`, which is four statements in order rather than a set of alternatives: `o.height = o.y2 - o.y` when a far edge is written beside a near one, `o.y = o.y2 - (o.height||0)` when it is written without one, and `o.y = o.yc - (o.height||0)/2` last of all. Because they are statements, a far edge *replaces* an encoded extent and a centre halves the replacement — so a mark centred on a band written as `y` and `y2` is placed against a height the specification never wrote down. The marks here write each combination on its own: a band centred by `yc`, a far edge with an extent and no near edge — on a rect, and on a symbol and a text, which resolve their position by a different route in this engine and had to be shown separately — the same pair on x, an encoded extent overwritten by a far edge beside it, and a **negative** width, which upstream keeps on the item and draws to the left of the anchor — only the bounding box is ordered.",
  "width": 420,
  "height": 220,
  "padding": 5,
  "background": "white",
  "data": [
    {
      "name": "t",
      "values": [
        {"c": 0, "lo": 40, "hi": 120},
        {"c": 1, "lo": 70, "hi": 160},
        {"c": 2, "lo": 20, "hi": 90}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "scales": [
    {"name": "x", "type": "point", "domain": {"data": "t", "field": "c"}, "range": [40, 380], "padding": 0.5}
  ],
